# quatricmorph TypeScript viz

- Keep modules focused: `viz/`, `util/`, `app/`, `gui/`.
- Prefer importing from specific modules (`viz/array2d.js`) over god-files when editing.
- Barrel files (`viz.ts`, `util.ts`) are compatibility shims — do not grow them with logic.
- Pure math/layout belongs in testable modules; avoid putting multiply logic only inside Three.js classes.
- Preserve GLSL1 on custom shaders unless migrating shaders deliberately.
- MVP UI must not promote attention/LoRA/nested expr/model loading (`VIZ-09`).
- After structural splits, verify cross-module exports (`toRange`, textures, etc.) still resolve.
